@startuml
title The `Int` binding-power ladder — LEVELS from declaration order, ties from `same`

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
  BorderColor #9CA3AF
}

rectangle "LOOSEST — binds least tightly" as TOP #FEE2E2

rectangle "**level 2** · mixfix · `c ? t : e` · **Tern**\n<latex>(\ell,r) = (3,2)</latex> · RIGHT-associative (declared `right`)\ndeclared FIRST among `Int` operators" as L_TERN #FEF3C7

rectangle "**level 4** · cross-category comparisons · operand `Int`, result `Bool`\n`==` `>` `<` `<=` `>=` `!=` — ALL <latex>(4,5)</latex> · LEFT-associative\nfive of the six carry `same`" as L_CMP #EDE9FE

rectangle "**level 6** · additive · LEFT-associative\n`+` `-` — both <latex>(6,7)</latex>\n`-` carries `same`" as L_ADD #DBEAFE

rectangle "**level 8** · multiplicative · LEFT-associative\n`*` `/` `%` — all <latex>(8,9)</latex>\n`/` and `%` carry `same`" as L_MUL #DBEAFE

rectangle "**level 10** · power · `^` · **PowInt**\n<latex>(\ell,r) = (11,10)</latex> · RIGHT-associative\n<latex>\ell > r</latex> is exactly what makes it right-associative" as L_POW #DCFCE7

rectangle "**levels 12, 14** · bitwise · LEFT-associative\n`bitor` <latex>(12,13)</latex> · `bitand` <latex>(14,15)</latex>\n`bitand` binds TIGHTER, mirroring `and`/`or`" as L_BIT #DBEAFE

rectangle "**level 16** · custom · `~` · **CustomOp**\n<latex>(16,17)</latex> · sole member of its level" as L_CUSTOM #DBEAFE

rectangle "**unary prefix** · `-` (**Neg**), `bitnot` (**BitNotInt**)\noperand floor <latex>= 19 = \max_{\mathrm{infix}} + 2</latex>" as L_PRE #DCFCE7

rectangle "**postfix** · `!` · **Fact**\n<latex>\ell = 21 = \max_{\mathrm{infix}} + 4</latex>" as L_POST #DCFCE7

rectangle "**atom** · literal / variable / `( … )` group\n`atomic_child_bp(Int)` <latex>= \max_{\mathrm{bp}} + 1</latex>" as L_ATOM #E0E7FF

rectangle "TIGHTEST — binds most tightly" as BOT #FEE2E2

TOP -down-> L_TERN
L_TERN -down-> L_CMP : next LEVEL (<latex>p := p+2</latex>)
L_CMP -down-> L_ADD : next LEVEL
L_ADD -down-> L_MUL : next LEVEL
L_MUL -down-> L_POW : next LEVEL
L_POW -down-> L_BIT : next LEVEL
L_BIT -down-> L_CUSTOM : next LEVEL
L_CUSTOM -down-> L_PRE : the +2 gap
L_PRE -down-> L_POST : the +4 gap
L_POST -down-> L_ATOM
L_ATOM -down-> BOT

note right of L_MUL
  **EQUAL PRECEDENCE, LEFT-TO-RIGHT.**
  All three offer <latex>\ell = 8</latex> and demand <latex>r = 9</latex>.
  Since <latex>8 < 9</latex>, none can be absorbed into
  another's right operand, so the chain nests
  LEFTWARD: `6 * 3 / 2` reads `(6 * 3) / 2` = 9.

  Before 2026-07-28 the counter advanced once
  per RULE, so `*` was <latex>(20,21)</latex> and `/` was
  <latex>(22,23)</latex> — `/` bound tighter and the same
  input evaluated to 6.
end note

note right of L_CMP
  Grouped by the OPERAND category, not the
  result: `EqInt : Bool` still occupies an
  `Int` slot, so declaring a comparison
  shifts every arithmetic LEVEL declared
  after it.
end note

note right of L_BIT
  **A TRAP THAT REMAINS.** `bitand` / `bitor`
  bind TIGHTER than `+` and `*` here — the
  opposite of C. `1 + 2 bitand 3` reads
  `1 + (2 bitand 3)`. Their placement relative
  to arithmetic is an OPEN QUESTION; only the
  inversion between them was corrected.
end note

note right of L_POW
  **RIGHT-ASSOCIATIVITY SURVIVES LEVELLING.**
  Precedence selects the level; associativity
  only decides which end of the level's two
  slots faces left. <latex>\min(11,10) = 10</latex> is the
  level, and <latex>\ell > r</latex> is the associativity.
  The two are independent, which is what lets
  Rholang's level 6 hold right-associative
  `matches` beside left-associative `==`.
end note

legend bottom
|= Component | = Meaning |
|<#DBEAFE> <latex>\ell</latex> (`left_bp`) | the floor an operator must CLEAR to be absorbed by the loop |
|<#DBEAFE> <latex>r</latex> (`right_bp`) | the floor the operator INSTALLS for its own right operand |
|<#EDE9FE> <latex>\min(\ell, r)</latex> | the PRECEDENCE LEVEL — equal for both associativities |
|<#DCFCE7> <latex>\ell < r</latex> | left-associative — the same operator cannot re-absorb |
|<#FEF3C7> <latex>\ell > r</latex> | right-associative — the same operator CAN re-absorb |
endlegend

@enduml
